1. What changed

I applied a two-line lifecycle fix in the worker-host teardown paths so disposal no longer short-circuits its own shutdown. In [engine-fast-worker-host.js:652](C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773525585541-26748/js/app/engine-fast-worker-host.js#L652) and [engine-fast-par-host.js:477](C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773525585541-26748/js/app/engine-fast-par-host.js#L477), `disposeAsync()` now awaits `stopAsync()` before setting `_disposed = true`. That lets the host send the worker `stop` message before termination instead of returning early and leaving `_ready`/pending requests to reject during teardown.

2. Which verification I ran

I ran:
- `node --check js/app/engine-fast-worker-host.js`
- `node --check js/app/engine-fast-par-host.js`

I also ran a focused inline Node harness that stubbed `Worker` and instantiated both `App.EventFastWorkerHost` and `App.EventFastParHost`, then verified that `disposeAsync()` posts `stop` before `terminate()` for the single-worker and partition-worker paths. That check passed with `dispose verification passed`.

3. Residual risk

Residual risk is low and limited to teardown sequencing. I did not run the hidden failure itself or a full engine suite, so this is verified at the host lifecycle level rather than end-to-end simulation parity. dt and event engine code paths were not modified.
